      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Both approaches offer distinct benefits depending on your specific educational goals and community values. A curriculum centered on national triumphs can build civic pride and a sense of shared identity among students. Conversely, one focusing on systemic injustices often better prepares students for critical analysis and democratic engagement in a diverse society. The most effective choice likely lies in a balanced approach that integrates both foundational values and an understanding of historical complexities.",
